WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:03.736
-There are just five,
count 'em, five days left

00:00:03.736 --> 00:00:05.004
in Donald Trump's presidency.

00:00:05.004 --> 00:00:07.407
His White House
is being boxed up.

00:00:07.407 --> 00:00:10.043
He's now the only president in
history to be impeached twice,

00:00:10.043 --> 00:00:12.612
and he's turning on some
of his closest allies.

00:00:12.612 --> 00:00:14.814
including his personal lawyer,
Rudy Giuliani.

00:00:14.814 --> 00:00:17.183
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:17.183 --> 00:00:20.987
♪♪

00:00:20.987 --> 00:00:23.456
Yesterday, Trump became
the first president in history

00:00:23.456 --> 00:00:24.524
to be impeached twice --

00:00:24.524 --> 00:00:26.392
this time, for inciting
an insurrection.

00:00:26.392 --> 00:00:29.262
And House Speaker Nancy Pelosi
made it official

00:00:29.262 --> 00:00:31.197
by immediately
signing the document,

00:00:31.197 --> 00:00:33.666
which will then be sent
to the Senate for a trial.

00:00:33.666 --> 00:00:37.636 line:0%
-Signing and certifying the bill
to make it official.

00:00:37.636 --> 00:00:39.472 line:0%
The Article of Impeachment

00:00:39.472 --> 00:00:42.108 line:0%
entitled
"Incitement of Insurrection."

00:00:42.108 --> 00:00:43.876 line:0%
There you see it, right there.

00:00:43.876 --> 00:00:45.645 line:0%
So it's a done deal, as far as

00:00:45.645 --> 00:00:47.513 line:0%
the House of Representatives
is concerned.

00:00:47.513 --> 00:00:49.082 line:0%
That document now will be

00:00:49.082 --> 00:00:51.351 line:0%
formally submitted
to the U.S. Senate,

00:00:51.351 --> 00:00:53.453 line:0%
where there will be a trial.

00:00:53.453 --> 00:00:55.388
-I don't think
Pelosi intended this,

00:00:55.388 --> 00:00:57.157
but it's a nice, little
troll of Trump

00:00:57.157 --> 00:00:58.925
to hold up the document
for the cameras,

00:00:58.925 --> 00:01:01.761
which was clearly one of his
favorite parts of the job.

00:01:01.761 --> 00:01:05.031
He loved signing things
and then showing them off,

00:01:05.031 --> 00:01:07.233
like he was doing story time
at the local library.

00:01:07.233 --> 00:01:09.035
[ As Trump ]
"Does everyone see the duck?

00:01:09.035 --> 00:01:11.804
Right there? And what
does the duck say, kids?

00:01:11.804 --> 00:01:15.508
Quack? I don't think so,
but it's your dime."

00:01:15.508 --> 00:01:18.278
So, the article will be sent
to the Senate for a trial,

00:01:18.278 --> 00:01:20.846
which could happen immediately,
if Mitch McConnell were willing

00:01:20.846 --> 00:01:22.649
to bring the Senate
back into session early.

00:01:22.649 --> 00:01:25.318
You might remember McConnell
leaking to reporters

00:01:25.318 --> 00:01:27.787
earlier this week that he was
pleased with impeachment

00:01:27.787 --> 00:01:29.655
and considering
voting to convict Trump.

00:01:29.655 --> 00:01:31.657 line:0%
Well, as usual with McConnell,

00:01:31.657 --> 00:01:33.493 line:0%
it turned out that was
bull[bleep].

00:01:33.493 --> 00:01:37.230 line:0%
-Mitch McConnell just sent a
letter to his Senate colleagues

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:40.599 line:0%
telling them that he will not
bring the Senate back early

00:01:40.599 --> 00:01:44.704 line:0%
before January 19th,
to reconvene the Senate.

00:01:44.704 --> 00:01:47.273 line:0%
Democrats wanted to have
a quick Senate trial,

00:01:47.273 --> 00:01:49.475 line:0%
have him convicted
before he leaves office.

00:01:49.475 --> 00:01:50.743 line:0%
That's not gonna happen.

00:01:50.743 --> 00:01:52.145 line:0%
-McConnell said he's undecided

00:01:52.145 --> 00:01:53.979 line:0%
about whether he'll
vote to convict Trump.

00:01:53.979 --> 00:01:55.215 line:0%
He said --

00:02:04.690 --> 00:02:07.160
-Of course McConnell tried
to polish his reputation

00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:09.128
by strategically
leaking to the media

00:02:09.128 --> 00:02:10.830
that he was considering
convicting Trump,

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:13.266
and then when it came time
to actually do something,

00:02:13.266 --> 00:02:15.034
chose the most craven
option available.

00:02:15.034 --> 00:02:16.702
Trusting Mitch McConnell
to do the right thing

00:02:16.702 --> 00:02:19.005
is like trusting Cujo
not to bite you.

00:02:19.005 --> 00:02:22.241
[ As McConnell ] "Oh, just give
me a treat. I won't bite.

00:02:22.241 --> 00:02:26.112
I'm a good boy.
Ha ha ha. Ha."

00:02:26.112 --> 00:02:27.513
[ Normal voice ]
Also, what arguments

00:02:27.513 --> 00:02:29.715
are you interested
in listening to?

00:02:29.715 --> 00:02:30.950
Arguments like these?

00:02:30.950 --> 00:02:32.619 line:0%
-It's not just about
impeachment anymore.

00:02:32.619 --> 00:02:33.953 line:0%
It's about canceling,
as I've said.

00:02:33.953 --> 00:02:35.054 line:0%
Canceling the President

00:02:35.054 --> 00:02:37.890 line:0%
and anyone that
disagrees with them.

00:02:37.890 --> 00:02:40.226 line:0%
The Ayatollah can tweet.
The President can't.

00:02:40.226 --> 00:02:42.128 line:0%
-Robert De Niro said

00:02:42.128 --> 00:02:44.397 line:0%
that he wanted to punch
the president in the face.

00:02:44.397 --> 00:02:46.566 line:0%
Madonna thought about
blowing up the White House.

00:02:46.566 --> 00:02:49.435 line:0%
Kathy Griffin held up a likeness

00:02:49.435 --> 00:02:52.171 line:0%
of the President's
beheaded head.

00:02:52.171 --> 00:02:53.639 line:0%
-Some have cited the metaphor

00:02:53.639 --> 00:02:55.241 line:0%
that the President
lit the flame.

00:02:55.241 --> 00:02:59.779 line:0%
Well, they lit actual flames.
Actual fires.

00:02:59.779 --> 00:03:03.683 line:0%
-Rather than actually helping
American people in this time,

00:03:03.683 --> 00:03:07.720 line:0%
we start impeachments that
further divide our country.

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:10.088 line:0%
I call bullcrap.

00:03:10.088 --> 00:03:11.424
-Oh, you call "bullcrap?"

00:03:11.424 --> 00:03:13.693
I didn't know you could invoke
your congressional power

00:03:13.693 --> 00:03:15.361
of declaring playground law.

00:03:15.361 --> 00:03:16.996
[ As Boebert ] "Not only
do I call bullcrap,

00:03:16.996 --> 00:03:19.431
I regret to inform the Speaker
the the impeachment

00:03:19.431 --> 00:03:23.302
has indeed bounced off of us
and now sticks to you!"

00:03:23.302 --> 00:03:24.803
[ Normal voice ] By the way,
that's Lauren Boebert,

00:03:24.803 --> 00:03:26.906
which also sounds
like a playground taunt.

00:03:26.906 --> 00:03:29.508
"I'm not a Boebert!"

00:03:29.508 --> 00:03:31.911
The congresswoman who has
bragged about her intention

00:03:31.911 --> 00:03:33.345
to carry a gun in Congress,

00:03:33.345 --> 00:03:35.581
and who defied
Capitol Police this week

00:03:35.581 --> 00:03:37.316
after they asked
to search her bag.

00:03:37.316 --> 00:03:38.784
And I just want to say,

00:03:38.784 --> 00:03:42.454
you think carrying a gun around
makes you more free?

00:03:42.454 --> 00:03:44.557
It makes everyone
else less free.

00:03:44.557 --> 00:03:46.892
You get to cosplay
as a Wild West sheriff,

00:03:46.892 --> 00:03:49.161
and everyone else has
to watch what they say,

00:03:49.161 --> 00:03:50.263
because they're afraid of you.

00:03:50.263 --> 00:03:52.632
That's not freedom,
it's intimidation.

00:03:52.632 --> 00:03:55.868
I'm sorry, it pains me to say
this, but I have no choice --

00:03:55.868 --> 00:03:59.705
I call bullcrap. Huhn-huhn-hunh.

00:03:59.705 --> 00:04:01.106
Also, let's go to Matt Gaetz.

00:04:01.106 --> 00:04:02.542
First of all,
your head looks like

00:04:02.542 --> 00:04:04.043
the ash tray I made
in third grade.

00:04:04.043 --> 00:04:06.078 line:0%
And more importantly,
what are you talking about,

00:04:06.078 --> 00:04:07.746 line:0%
"Democrats lit actual flames?"

00:04:07.746 --> 00:04:09.015 line:0%
Are you insane?

00:04:09.015 --> 00:04:11.317 line:0%
It was Trump supporters who
stormed the Capitol,

00:04:11.317 --> 00:04:13.218 line:0%
ransacked the place,
left five people dead,

00:04:13.218 --> 00:04:16.088 line:0%
and tried to capture or
murder elected officials.

00:04:16.088 --> 00:04:17.657 line:0%
Just a note, Gaetz.

00:04:17.657 --> 00:04:19.358
When you scream, you don't sound

00:04:19.358 --> 00:04:20.826
as righteous
as you think you do.

00:04:20.826 --> 00:04:23.696
You sound like an angry
frat dude telling the Dean

00:04:23.696 --> 00:04:27.700
why it was actually Sigma Chi's
fault the Greek Row burned down.

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:29.936
[ As Gaetz ] "We had a small,
controlled fire pit

00:04:29.936 --> 00:04:32.170
for our annual beach-themed
summer party,

00:04:32.170 --> 00:04:35.941
but Sigma Chi lit actual flames
for their pig roast!

00:04:35.941 --> 00:04:40.613
Also, they drew eyebrows
on our house dog!

00:04:40.613 --> 00:04:46.118
Now Rufus looks like a dick!"

00:04:46.118 --> 00:04:47.352
[ Normal voice ]
Although, I have to say,

00:04:47.352 --> 00:04:49.521
my favorite example
of GOP psychosis yesterday

00:04:49.521 --> 00:04:51.857
came from
Marjorie Taylor Greene,

00:04:51.857 --> 00:04:55.561
whose name sounds like a child
actor from ABC'S TGIF lineup,

00:04:55.561 --> 00:04:58.497
but is unfortunately a GOP
member of Congress

00:04:58.497 --> 00:05:01.367
who has promoted the QAnon
conspiracy theory,

00:05:01.367 --> 00:05:03.802
which the FBI has called
a domestic terror threat,

00:05:03.802 --> 00:05:05.872
said there's an Islamic invasion
in the government,

00:05:05.872 --> 00:05:08.006
held up an AR-15
in a campaign ad,

00:05:08.006 --> 00:05:10.576
endangered her colleagues by
refusing to wear a mask

00:05:10.576 --> 00:05:12.145
last week during
the Capitol lockdown,

00:05:12.145 --> 00:05:14.013
and who voted to overturn
the election results

00:05:14.013 --> 00:05:15.414
even after the riot last week.

00:05:15.414 --> 00:05:18.684 line:0%
-Democrats are on record
supporting violence

00:05:18.684 --> 00:05:22.488 line:0%
when it serves their cause,
in their own words,

00:05:22.488 --> 00:05:25.157 line:0%
on social media,
on interviews,

00:05:25.157 --> 00:05:28.027 line:0%
and on fundraising platforms.

00:05:28.027 --> 00:05:31.197
-That's right, she's wearing
a mask that says "censored,

00:05:31.197 --> 00:05:32.665
in case you couldn't read it

00:05:32.665 --> 00:05:35.568
because of
the microphone in the way.

00:05:35.568 --> 00:05:37.036
You know how dumb you look?

00:05:37.036 --> 00:05:38.637
You're speaking on the floor
of the House of Representatives

00:05:38.637 --> 00:05:40.606
and being broadcast
on national television.

00:05:40.606 --> 00:05:43.108
It's like Lebron James
wearing a shirt that says,

00:05:43.108 --> 00:05:44.443
"Play me, coach!"

00:05:44.443 --> 00:05:45.778
These people will
stop at nothing

00:05:45.778 --> 00:05:47.279
to make themselves
feel like victims.

00:05:47.279 --> 00:05:48.448
It's all they have.

00:05:48.448 --> 00:05:49.882
It's the core of their
political ideology.

00:05:49.882 --> 00:05:51.817
They have no actual
policies or principles.

00:05:51.817 --> 00:05:54.686
They just spin wild fantasies
of persecution,

00:05:54.686 --> 00:05:57.890
and that's basically what Fox
News has been doing 24/7.

00:05:57.890 --> 00:06:00.926 line:0%
-We impeached the president
today without any evidence.

00:06:00.926 --> 00:06:02.694 line:0%
It's just sheer hatred.

00:06:02.694 --> 00:06:04.630 line:0%
If this becomes the norm,

00:06:04.630 --> 00:06:07.032 line:0%
be careful what
you wish for today.

00:06:07.032 --> 00:06:09.102 line:0%
Under this theory,
the radical left --

00:06:09.102 --> 00:06:12.371 line:0%
if you can impeach a president
after they're out of office,

00:06:12.371 --> 00:06:13.940 line:0%
why don't we impeach
George Washington?

00:06:13.940 --> 00:06:15.107 line:0%
He owned slaves.

00:06:15.107 --> 00:06:16.274 line:0%
Where does it stop?

00:06:16.274 --> 00:06:18.043
-You see, the point is

00:06:18.043 --> 00:06:20.412
to hold Trump accountable
for his actions

00:06:20.412 --> 00:06:23.082
and disqualify him from
holding office again.

00:06:23.082 --> 00:06:25.284
Washington is already
disqualified

00:06:25.284 --> 00:06:27.586
on account of, spoiler alert,
being dead.

00:06:27.586 --> 00:06:30.156
These guys love to just
make up insane fantasies,

00:06:30.156 --> 00:06:31.591
because it's all they have.

00:06:31.591 --> 00:06:34.360
They have no policy goals,
just scary, imagined grievances

00:06:34.360 --> 00:06:35.628
to keep their base in line.

00:06:35.628 --> 00:06:37.096
[ As Graham ] "Next, they're
gonna try to impeach

00:06:37.096 --> 00:06:39.698
George Washington or
Thomas Jefferson

00:06:39.698 --> 00:06:42.301
or Paul Blart, or maybe
they'll send Ernest to Jail.

00:06:42.301 --> 00:06:44.937
Or, hell, even worse, maybe
they'll break Ernest out of jail

00:06:44.937 --> 00:06:46.705
so his crime spree can continue.

00:06:46.705 --> 00:06:49.108
I call bull crap, Sean."

00:06:49.108 --> 00:06:50.609
[ Normal voice ] So, I guess
those are the kind of arguments

00:06:50.609 --> 00:06:52.644
McConnell wants to hear
in the impeachment trial.

00:06:52.644 --> 00:06:55.014
But even if McConnell
delays the trial

00:06:55.014 --> 00:06:56.582
until after Trump leaves office,

00:06:56.582 --> 00:06:59.652
it's still urgently necessary,
because if they convict him,

00:06:59.652 --> 00:07:02.621
they can also disqualify him
from holding office ever again.

00:07:02.621 --> 00:07:04.924
And you know Trump will
run again if he can.

00:07:04.924 --> 00:07:06.458
Right now he's sitting
in the White House,

00:07:06.458 --> 00:07:08.761
stewing by himself,
watching as they literally

00:07:08.761 --> 00:07:10.896
load his [bleep] into boxes.

00:07:10.896 --> 00:07:11.931 line:0%
-Now, as the Trump
administration

00:07:11.931 --> 00:07:13.165 line:0%
enters its final stage,

00:07:13.165 --> 00:07:15.501 line:0%
the first sign of
the end of a presidency --

00:07:15.501 --> 00:07:17.770 line:0%
a moving van
outside the West Wing.

00:07:17.770 --> 00:07:19.838 line:0%
Stacks of moving boxes
were being delivered

00:07:19.838 --> 00:07:22.575 line:0%
to the Eisenhower
Executive Office Building.

00:07:22.575 --> 00:07:24.476 line:0%
The office will be
undergoing a deep cleaning

00:07:24.476 --> 00:07:27.012 line:0%
just before
President-elect Biden moves in.

00:07:27.012 --> 00:07:29.181 line:0%
There are very few people
left in this building,

00:07:29.181 --> 00:07:30.782 line:0%
and I can tell you that
having just walked through

00:07:30.782 --> 00:07:32.418 line:0%
the West Wing in the last hour,

00:07:32.418 --> 00:07:34.386 line:0%
the very few people
who are still here

00:07:34.386 --> 00:07:37.489 line:0%
are currently packing up
boxes in their offices.

00:07:37.489 --> 00:07:39.225
-Trump's still president
for five more days,

00:07:39.225 --> 00:07:42.795
but that place is emptier than
a rest stop Cinnabon at 3:00 AM.

00:07:42.795 --> 00:07:45.131
And, man, I didn't think
anything could be more cathartic

00:07:45.131 --> 00:07:46.766
than Trump losing
and getting impeached twice,

00:07:46.766 --> 00:07:49.201
but actually, seeing the boxes
is pretty great.

00:07:49.201 --> 00:07:51.470
Love to imagine Trump piling
all his stuff into crates --

00:07:51.470 --> 00:07:54.707
his oversize suits,
his ties that are so long

00:07:54.707 --> 00:07:57.976
that no matter how you pack
them, a little bit pokes out.

00:07:57.976 --> 00:07:59.678
And I sure hope someone
is watching him pack,

00:07:59.678 --> 00:08:02.281
because he's definitely
going to try to steal stuff.

00:08:02.281 --> 00:08:04.883
"Sir, why is the bust of Lincoln
being packed away?"

00:08:04.883 --> 00:08:07.720
[ As Trump ] "Uh, what?
No, this is mine from home.

00:08:07.720 --> 00:08:10.156
I brought it. It's not
actually Lincoln.

00:08:10.156 --> 00:08:15.327
It's my uncle, um...
Beard Trump.

00:08:15.327 --> 00:08:17.696
Mel?

00:08:17.696 --> 00:08:21.633
Mel, I need you
to vouch for the bust.

00:08:21.633 --> 00:08:23.969
Mel?

00:08:23.969 --> 00:08:26.439
We -- Mel?

00:08:26.439 --> 00:08:28.373
What?

00:08:28.373 --> 00:08:29.909
When did she leave?"

00:08:32.678 --> 00:08:34.947
By the way, we we wrote
this joke right here,

00:08:34.947 --> 00:08:36.682
about stealing the bust
this morning,

00:08:36.682 --> 00:08:40.486
and then as often happens
in the Trump administration,

00:08:40.486 --> 00:08:42.154
this afternoon,
this went down.

00:08:42.154 --> 00:08:44.223 line:0%
-We're seeing what looks
like moving day over here

00:08:44.223 --> 00:08:45.258 line:0%
at the White House.

00:08:45.258 --> 00:08:46.792 line:0%
You're seeing things, items,

00:08:46.792 --> 00:08:48.160 line:0%
coming and going
from the West Wing.

00:08:48.160 --> 00:08:50.930 line:0%
We saw Larry Kudlow
leaving earlier today.

00:08:50.930 --> 00:08:54.400 line:0%
Here's some video of
a bust of Abraham Lincoln

00:08:54.400 --> 00:08:56.969 line:0%
being carried out
of the West Wing.

00:08:56.969 --> 00:09:00.005
-[ Chuckles ]

00:09:00.005 --> 00:09:01.073
You know, who knows?

00:09:01.073 --> 00:09:03.208
Maybe they're Purelling them,
you know?

00:09:03.208 --> 00:09:05.277
Maybe they didn't want
even a bust of Lincoln

00:09:05.277 --> 00:09:07.780
to see a grown man cry
in the Oval Office.

00:09:07.780 --> 00:09:11.016
Or maybe, it's an O.J. situation
all over again.

00:09:11.016 --> 00:09:12.217
That's right.

00:09:12.217 --> 00:09:13.919
Just like O.J.,
they're going to nail Trump

00:09:13.919 --> 00:09:16.822
for stealing memorabilia.

00:09:16.822 --> 00:09:18.256
As the boxes arrive
and the specter

00:09:18.256 --> 00:09:20.159
of a second impeachment trial
hangs over him,

00:09:20.159 --> 00:09:21.360
it's hard to fully articulate

00:09:21.360 --> 00:09:22.928
just how much of
a failure and disgrace

00:09:22.928 --> 00:09:24.497
Trump will be
in the eyes of history.

00:09:24.497 --> 00:09:26.498
Even if you just go
by the numbers alone,

00:09:26.498 --> 00:09:28.067
Trump lost
the popular vote twice,

00:09:28.067 --> 00:09:29.701
both times by millions of votes.

00:09:29.701 --> 00:09:30.836
Got impeached twice.

00:09:30.836 --> 00:09:33.105
He lost the House by
a record margin in 2018,

00:09:33.105 --> 00:09:36.342
and he lost the Senate in 2021
by losing two seats

00:09:36.342 --> 00:09:39.144
in what has for a long time
been a reliably red state.

00:09:39.144 --> 00:09:41.580
Do you know how unpopular
you have to be as a Republican

00:09:41.580 --> 00:09:43.348
to go 0-2 in Georgia?

00:09:43.348 --> 00:09:45.484
Imagine if Democrats
lost control of the Senate

00:09:45.484 --> 00:09:46.986
by going 0-2 in California.

00:09:46.986 --> 00:09:50.189
James Carville would be on MSNBC
doing tequila shots,

00:09:50.189 --> 00:09:52.091
crying into one of
his squashed-up hats

00:09:52.091 --> 00:09:54.093
I'm assuming he stole
from the dumpster

00:09:54.093 --> 00:09:55.760
behind a Louisiana thrift store.

00:09:55.760 --> 00:09:56.761
What's with this guy?

00:09:56.761 --> 00:09:58.497
He always looks
like a little kid

00:09:58.497 --> 00:10:00.732
who wished on a monkey's paw
to be a grown-up.

00:10:00.732 --> 00:10:02.033
[ As Carville ]
"Ah, cotswaddle!

00:10:02.033 --> 00:10:03.736
Not like this!"

00:10:03.736 --> 00:10:08.107
Oh, you win this round,
monkey paw!"

00:10:08.107 --> 00:10:09.308
Oh, and on top of all that,

00:10:09.308 --> 00:10:11.777
Trump has also overseen
the needless deaths

00:10:11.777 --> 00:10:14.012
of hundreds of thousands
of Americans,

00:10:14.012 --> 00:10:16.682
and will leave office
with 3 million fewer jobs

00:10:16.682 --> 00:10:18.016
than when he took office --

00:10:18.016 --> 00:10:20.418
by far the worst jobs record
in modern U.S. history.

00:10:20.418 --> 00:10:22.087
Even if everything else
about him is forgotten

00:10:22.087 --> 00:10:23.255
100 years from now,

00:10:23.255 --> 00:10:24.857
those numbers will be
remembered forever.

00:10:24.857 --> 00:10:26.958
When it's time to do
oral reports in history class,

00:10:26.958 --> 00:10:28.494
every student
will want Trump

00:10:28.494 --> 00:10:30.362
because it'll be
the easiest assignment.

00:10:30.362 --> 00:10:32.898
"Michael, can you give us
FDR's accomplishments?"

00:10:32.898 --> 00:10:34.799
"Well, he stopped
the Great Depression

00:10:34.799 --> 00:10:36.001
and won World War II."

00:10:36.001 --> 00:10:38.003
"Okay, but you forgot
a few things, so, B-.

00:10:38.003 --> 00:10:39.771
And Timmy,
can you tell us about

00:10:39.771 --> 00:10:42.307
Donald Trump's
accomplishments?"

00:10:42.307 --> 00:10:43.909
"He was friends
with Grimace."

00:10:43.909 --> 00:10:46.811
"A-plus, Timmy.
You got it all.

00:10:46.811 --> 00:10:48.914
You could learn a thing
or two from Timmy, Michael."

00:10:48.914 --> 00:10:51.317
And yet, the harsh reality
that we must reckon with

00:10:51.317 --> 00:10:53.018
is that,
with only a few exceptions,

00:10:53.018 --> 00:10:54.820
the Republican Party
spent the last four years

00:10:54.820 --> 00:10:56.622
colluding with
this evil.

00:10:56.622 --> 00:10:57.923
And they knew
it was evil.

00:10:57.923 --> 00:11:00.192
Ted Cruz, Marco Rubio,
Rick Perry, Lindsey Graham,

00:11:00.192 --> 00:11:01.526
Nikki Haley --
they all saw it.

00:11:01.526 --> 00:11:04.129
They even warned us about it
during the primaries --

00:11:04.129 --> 00:11:06.031
before deciding to shame
themselves, and join in.

00:11:06.031 --> 00:11:08.967
And even now, the vast majority
of the Republican Party

00:11:08.967 --> 00:11:11.303
remains in the grip
of a mass delusion

00:11:11.303 --> 00:11:12.905
it refuses to shake --

00:11:12.905 --> 00:11:14.940
the delusion that motivated
last week's attack --

00:11:14.940 --> 00:11:15.974
that Trump
won the election,

00:11:15.974 --> 00:11:17.409
and that Joe Biden
is illegitimate.

00:11:17.409 --> 00:11:20.045
These people have devoted
themselves to the Trump cult.

00:11:20.045 --> 00:11:21.980
But if there's one thing
we've learned, it's that,

00:11:21.980 --> 00:11:23.782
no matter how much loyalty
you show him,

00:11:23.782 --> 00:11:26.351
he's never, ever,
ever gonna repay it.

00:11:26.351 --> 00:11:28.120
I mean, look what he did
to Mike Pence,

00:11:28.120 --> 00:11:29.688
or how about
his personal lawyer,

00:11:29.688 --> 00:11:32.558
Rudy Giuliani, the man who
single-handedly led the charge

00:11:32.558 --> 00:11:34.993
to get the election overturned
by flying from state to state,

00:11:34.993 --> 00:11:37.329
holding press conferences
at landscaping companies,

00:11:37.329 --> 00:11:40.332
and meeting with every
drunk loon he could find?

00:11:40.332 --> 00:11:41.600
Obviously,
it was all a grift.

00:11:41.600 --> 00:11:44.436
Rudy was reportedly
billing Trump $20,000 a day.

00:11:44.436 --> 00:11:46.505
And guess what?
Trump doesn't want to pay.

00:11:46.505 --> 00:11:49.208 line:0%
-President Trump is reportedly
taking out his frustrations

00:11:49.208 --> 00:11:51.376 line:0%
on his personal attorney,
Rudy Giuliani,

00:11:51.376 --> 00:11:54.413 line:0%
by refusing to pay him
for his legal services.

00:11:54.413 --> 00:11:57.382 line:0%
The Washington Post is reporting
that President Trump

00:11:57.382 --> 00:11:59.017 line:0%
is trying to
stiff Giuliani,

00:11:59.017 --> 00:12:00.485 line:0%
who has spent
the past few months

00:12:00.485 --> 00:12:03.789 line:0%
traveling the country, and
spreading conspiracy theories

00:12:03.789 --> 00:12:06.258 line:0%
about the November election
on behalf of the president.

00:12:06.258 --> 00:12:10.629 line:0%
Giuliani is seeking
$20,000 per day in fees.

00:12:10.629 --> 00:12:13.665 line:0%
The newspaper says the president
has not only refused to pay

00:12:13.665 --> 00:12:15.400 line:0%
Giuliani's legal fees,

00:12:15.400 --> 00:12:18.003 line:0%
but has told aides that
all reimbursement requests

00:12:18.003 --> 00:12:22.040 line:0%
for travel and other expenses
need to go through him.

00:12:22.040 --> 00:12:23.975
-Impeachment was great,
but there really is

00:12:23.975 --> 00:12:27.145
no more perfect way for this
to end than Trump stiffing Rudy.

00:12:27.145 --> 00:12:29.081
The guy spent all that time
flying to state capitols,

00:12:29.081 --> 00:12:30.716
rounding up witnesses
from the bars

00:12:30.716 --> 00:12:32.752
at TGI Fridays
and Buffalo Wild Wings,

00:12:32.752 --> 00:12:34.486
and now, Trump won't even
reimburse him.

00:12:34.486 --> 00:12:37.289
[ As Trump ]
"Also, you owe me for the time
I called into the hearing.

00:12:37.289 --> 00:12:38.791
It went over
on minutes.

00:12:38.791 --> 00:12:41.560
Because, Rudy, you're not
friends, and you're not family,

00:12:41.560 --> 00:12:43.228
so those minutes
are costly."

00:12:43.228 --> 00:12:45.864
[ Normal voice ]
And poor Rudy needed that money
for the hair transplant.

00:12:45.864 --> 00:12:47.098
[ As Giuliani ]
"Please, boss, I'm begging you,

00:12:47.098 --> 00:12:49.734
don't make me go back
to the mud water."

00:12:49.734 --> 00:12:51.370
[ Normal voice ]
This is like the end
of "The Sixth Sense,"

00:12:51.370 --> 00:12:52.638
but instead
of Bruce Willis

00:12:52.638 --> 00:12:54.373
realizing he's been dead
the whole time,

00:12:54.373 --> 00:12:56.908
it's Donald Trump realizing
that Rudy has,

00:12:56.908 --> 00:13:00.112
the whole time,
been a bad lawyer.

00:13:00.112 --> 00:13:01.613
[ As Trump ]
"Oh, no.

00:13:01.613 --> 00:13:03.015
Wait a second.

00:13:05.583 --> 00:13:09.654
He was a bad lawyer."

00:13:09.654 --> 00:13:12.591
[ Normal voice ]
Nothing Trump or Republicans
say or do from here on out

00:13:12.591 --> 00:13:15.460
should be taken seriously,
unless they uniformly

00:13:15.460 --> 00:13:17.696
and unequivocally
acknowledge the reality

00:13:17.696 --> 00:13:19.264
that the election
was not rigged,

00:13:19.264 --> 00:13:21.934
and that Joe Biden won,
and apologize for their roles

00:13:21.934 --> 00:13:24.269
in spreading lies
and conspiracy theories

00:13:24.269 --> 00:13:26.138
fomenting the insurrection
we saw last week.

00:13:26.138 --> 00:13:28.206
Unfortunately,
as we saw yesterday,

00:13:28.206 --> 00:13:31.209
too many of them have walled
themselves off from reality.

00:13:31.209 --> 00:13:33.578
They live in a deranged
fantasy world of grievance,

00:13:33.578 --> 00:13:35.047
and victimhood, lies,

00:13:35.047 --> 00:13:36.681
conspiracy theories,
and...

00:13:36.681 --> 00:13:37.783
-Bullcrap.

00:13:37.783 --> 00:13:39.618
This has been
"A Closer Look."

